// Ordering two strings: -1, 0 or 1.
//
// **There is no `<` on strings in this language** -- `"abc" < "abd"` is
// `error: cannot order string and string` -- so sorting, binary search and any
// ordered map are impossible without this function. That is why it is here even
// though `==` exists.
//
// The order is by byte code, so it is ASCII order: every uppercase letter sorts
// before every lowercase one. It is not a collation and does not pretend to be.
//
// The end-of-string sentinel does the length comparison for free: charat answers
// -1 past the end, which is below every real byte, so a prefix sorts before what
// extends it and two ends compare equal. No separate length test is needed, and
// that is the whole reason this is two small functions rather than four.
//
// It alternates charat between two strings, so it pays a strlen per byte (see
// scan/eq.id). For sorting a list of short names that is invisible; for
// comparing two 100 KB documents it is the wrong tool.
//
// The parameters are `s` and `txt` rather than the `a`, `b` that read better,
// because `a` and `b` are the *int* operands of fx_min/fx_max and a name keeps
// one type across the whole program -- imported trees included. Writing
// `str_cmp(string a, string b)` produced twenty-eight errors, every one of them
// reported inside core/math, for a declaration made here. NAMES.md §2 is the
// list that stops that happening twice.

str_cmp(string idstd_s, string idstd_txt) {
  int idstd_i = idstd_str_cmp_run(idstd_s, idstd_txt, 0);
  int idstd_ret_i = idstd_str_cmp_sign(idstd_s, idstd_txt, idstd_i);
} return int idstd_ret_i;
("abc", "abd"):(-1)
("abc", "abc"):(0)
("abd", "abc"):(1)

// The sign of the difference at the point idstd_str_cmp_run stopped -- split out
// so str_cmp's own block stays inside the action limit.
idstd_str_cmp_sign(string idstd_s, string idstd_txt, int idstd_i) {
  int idstd_charat_v = charat(idstd_s, idstd_i);
  int idstd_charat_v2 = charat(idstd_txt, idstd_i);
  int idstd_ret_i = fx_sign(idstd_charat_v - idstd_charat_v2);
} return int idstd_ret_i;
("abc", "abd", 2):(-1)
("abc", "abc", 3):(0)

// The first index at which the two differ, or the index of the shared end.
idstd_str_cmp_run(string idstd_s, string idstd_txt, int idstd_i) {
  while (charat(idstd_s, idstd_i) >= 0 && charat(idstd_s, idstd_i) = charat(idstd_txt, idstd_i)) {
    idstd_i = idstd_i + 1;
  }
} return int idstd_i;
("abc", "abd", 0):(2)
("abc", "abc", 0):(3)
